<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 29,970,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 29,970,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 02/26/97    02/19/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 29,970,000  30,864,000    26,257,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	 268,124     127,996	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	35,324,000  35,324,000    33,981,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,516,775  35,516,775	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   02/26/97    02/19/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   5,301,000   5,524,000     4,592,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    5,059,000   5,285,000     4,571,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  5,064,000   5,012,000     4,278,000</p>
<p> South Central    3,139,000   3,312,000     2,603,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  4,287,000   4,307,000     3,355,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,155,000   5,169,000     4,914,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,965,000   2,255,000     1,944,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	29,970,000  30,864,000    26,257,000</p>
